# Configure GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY in .env (server-only), enable Google Routes API
# with billing, then start the backend with: bun run dev:server
# Both /route and /api/route are supported. The Vite proxy uses /api/route.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Driving route in San Jose, Costa Rica
POST {{baseUrl}}/route
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "origin": { "lat": 9.9325, "lng": -84.08 },
  "destination": { "lat": 9.935, "lng": -84.053 }
}

# Illustrative response only; distance, duration and geometry vary:
# { "duration": "165s", "distanceMeters": 772, "encodedPolyline": "ipkcFfichVnP@j@BLoFVwM{E?" }
# duration uses Google's seconds-string format, including optional fractions.
# Decode encodedPolyline using the map's geometry library to draw it.
# Errors: { "code": "ROUTE_NOT_FOUND", "message": "..." }
# 422: invalid input; 404: no driving route; 429: local/provider rate limit;
# 503: missing key or Google rejection; 502: network/upstream/malformed reply;
# 504: timeout (8 seconds, including reading the body).
# 429 includes Retry-After in seconds. No automatic retries are billed.
# Budget: 60 calls/minute per app process, shared across all visitors/aliases.
# For multiple replicas, enforce a shared limit in the gateway or shared store.
